From a8098f8bf6c9bebcc7b51f65d8549cc8788641c8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AyeedShaikh <ayeedxec@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 11:01:24 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] toybox: Send a correct ICMP checksum in ping

pingchksum() returned the sum, not its complement, and its carry test
added 1 when the sum before a word was 0.  A Linux ICMP datagram socket
computes the checksum again, so the value did not go out there.  A
FreeBSD raw socket sends the ICMPv4 checksum of the program as it is,
so the receiver dropped each echo request ("bad checksum") and ping
127.0.0.1 lost every packet.  Test the carry with ">" and return the
complement, as RFC 1071 says.

The project freebsd-android-native carries this patch (owner decision
O17).
---
 toys/net/ping.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/toys/net/ping.c b/toys/net/ping.c
index a25d0aa..f209cc2 100644
--- a/toys/net/ping.c
+++ b/toys/net/ping.c
@@ -81,11 +81,11 @@ static unsigned short pingchksum(unsigned short *data, int len)
   while (len>0) {
     d = *data++;
     if (len == 1) d &= 255<<IS_BIG_ENDIAN;
-    if (d >= (u += d)) u++;
+    if (d > (u += d)) u++;
     len -= 2;
   }
 
-  return u;
+  return ~u;
 }
 
 static int xrecvmsgwait(int fd, struct msghdr *msg, int flag,
